# spark_of_talent — the first magic quest, converted from MagicTutorial.cs
#
# ⚠ THIS FILE OWNS DANIEL PAULS' ENTIRE CONVERSATION.
# One DIALOGUE block per npcId across the whole quests/ folder: each import regenerates
# Dialogue_danielpauls.asset wholesale, so a second file declaring DIALOGUE danielpauls would
# clobber this one. Every future Daniel Pauls quest adds its nodes to THIS file, gated on its own
# quest id — see daniel_pauls_quest_one.quest, which deliberately carries no DIALOGUE block.
#
# The "done" node is the post-quest state and is expected to grow: as Daniel gains more quests,
# add a new gated choice on NODE start rather than rewriting his farewell.
#
# ⚠ spark_of_talent is a SAVE KEY. It is the id MagicTutorial has always used and existing saves
# hold it. Never change it.
#
# Requires the ActiveAtStage gate and the TEACHSPARK directive — see
# docs/reference/QUEST_TEXT_FORMAT.md.

QUEST spark_of_talent
TITLE: Spark of Talent
GIVER: Daniel Pauls
LOCATION: London

# Stage 0 — kill the geezer. under_housed is the QuestActor.Key stamped on Enemy_UnderHoused.
STAGE KILL under_housed x1
OBJECTIVE: Daniel Pauls reckons the sparks are real magic. Walk into the city and sound out the twitchy geezer he pointed you at.

# Stage 1 — MANUAL, not TALKTO, deliberately. A TalkTo final stage completes the quest on the
# interact, BEFORE any choice is picked, which would flip the gates mid-conversation and skip the
# reward beat entirely. The dialogue's COMPLETE: below is what ends this quest.
STAGE MANUAL
OBJECTIVE: You're crackling with it. Get back to Daniel Pauls and tell him what happened.

# No payout: the reward is Spark itself, taught by the TEACHSPARK choice. A non-zero reward here
# would also retro-pay every existing save that already holds this quest complete.
REWARD
POUNDS: 0
XP: 0

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

DIALOGUE danielpauls

# Daniel opens with the same line at every beat; which branch is offered depends on quest state.
# Exactly one of the four gated choices can ever be visible at once.
NODE start
SPEAKER: danielpauls
SPEAK: David Blaine was my 3rd ever student. Second was a fella named Jesus. Now he didn't learn too much, I didn't know spanish and he wasn't great with English but he was a good trier.
CHOICE Uh what? -> offer_open
GATE: not-started spark_of_talent
CHOICE Okay okay! -> nudge
GATE: stage spark_of_talent 0
CHOICE Cheers I guess. -> reward
GATE: stage spark_of_talent 1
CHOICE Fine. -> done
GATE: complete spark_of_talent
CHOICE End Conversation.

NODE offer_open
SPEAKER: danielpauls
SPEAK: HEY YOU! I can sense it, you've got it. Do me a favour and I'll change your life!
CHOICE What you on about? What you up to? -> research
CHOICE Not now, weirdo.

NODE research
SPEAKER: danielpauls
SPEAK: There's been a few suspect events. Sparks and bangs, strange folk acting aloof.
CHOICE Actually — saw a bloke get zapped by some smackhead by the Jones' last week. Thought I'd had some dodgy bud. -> sendoff
GRANT: spark_of_talent
CHOICE Right. I'll leave you to it.

NODE sendoff
SPEAKER: danielpauls
SPEAK: Haha! That wasn't the bud, son. That was magic. Please, do me a kindness. Find the oddball and have a word for me.

NODE nudge
SPEAKER: danielpauls
SPEAK: Come on! Get after him!

NODE reward
SPEAKER: danielpauls
SPEAK: Let's have it! I knew you had it in you, you've got the gift!
CHOICE So... what happens now? -> teach
TEACHSPARK
COMPLETE: spark_of_talent

NODE teach
SPEAKER: danielpauls
SPEAK: Right, now I invoke the 7 secret corners of the magic circle....... GUH........ feel that? Give it a name if you want, then shout it out and try it!

NODE done
SPEAKER: danielpauls
SPEAK: Careful where you sling spells lad. Johnny Law comes a knocking if you're to liberal with the lightening.

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

DIALOGUE underhoused
# Both accusations are gated to stage 0, so once he is dead — and after the quest is over — the
# node has no visible exit and DialogueManager supplies its own escape button. A player who talks
# to him before taking the quest just hears his opening line and leaves.

NODE start
SPEAKER: underhoused
SPEAK: ...You what? I ain't done nothin'. Move along, yeah?
CHOICE Saw you near the Jones' the other night. Bit of a light show, weren't it? -> accuse_lightshow
GATE: stage spark_of_talent 0
CHOICE Someone's been zappin' folk round here. That you, mate? -> accuse_direct
GATE: stage spark_of_talent 0

NODE accuse_lightshow
SPEAKER: underhoused
SPEAK: I don't— I don't know what you're on about. Back off. I'm tellin' you, BACK OFF—

NODE accuse_direct
SPEAKER: underhoused
SPEAK: Nnnh— you shouldn't've said that. You shouldn't've—
